ladder.draft.complaint:
I am reporting intimate content of me that was shared online without my consent.
On {date}, I reported it to {platform}. It has not been removed.
Link: {link}
My Asmita case reference: {ref}
Sharing such content without consent may be an offence under section 66E of the Information Technology Act, 2000 and section 77 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023.
I request that the content be removed and that action be taken against the person who shared it.

ladder.draft.appeal:
I am appealing under Rule 3A of the Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021, because {platform} has not removed intimate content of me that was shared without my consent.
I reported it to {platform} on {date}. {outcome}
Under Rule 3(2)(b) of the same Rules, on a complaint by the person shown in such content or someone acting for her, a platform must take all reasonable and practicable measures to remove it within two hours.
Link: {link}
My Asmita case reference: {ref}
I request the Committee to direct {platform} to remove the content.
